      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =0-6+15 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
